<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Ryswick</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1697">1697</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Peace of Ryswick · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war">Nine Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Ryswick, signed in September and October 1697 at Rijswijk near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-hague">The Hague</a>, ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war">Nine Years' War</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the Grand Alliance. France returned most of its gains since 1679 but kept Strasbourg, and recognised William III as king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> accepted French possession of the western third of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a>, which became the colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-domingue">Saint-Domingue</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-ryswick.jpg" alt="Treaty of Ryswick" width="320" height="272" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: engraver is Jan van Vianen, whose name appears in the lower left corner · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rijswijk_Netherlands_-_Huis_ter_Nieuwburg_by_P._Schenck.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
